      "title": "Albanese looks for reset on world stage as ‘spot fires burn’ domestically and likely interest rate hike looms",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/31/albanese-reset-world-stage-economic-spot-fires-rba-interest-rate-decision",
      "description": "<p>The prime minister will speak with King Charles and others at the Commonwealth heads of government meeting in Antigua and Barbuda</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>As “summit season” begins, reaffirming ties with fellow leaders on the world stage could be a circuit breaker for Anthony Albanese amid domestic and economic woes, analysts have said.</p><p>But a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/grogonomics/2026/oct/29/the-rba-has-primed-the-market-for-an-interest-rate-rise-but-what-will-it-mean-for-unemployment\">likely interest rate hike</a> triggered by <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/28/inflation-rate-australia-2026-number-data-consumer-price-index-cpi-release\">higher-than-expected inflation</a> while the prime minister is overseas will make his job – and the treasurer’s – even harder.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/31/albanese-reset-world-stage-economic-spot-fires-rba-interest-rate-decision\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-31T02:24:10"
    },
    {
      "title": "A top-secret spy mission, a decades-old scandal – and the Austin Powers-esque saga to lift the lid",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/31/timor-leste-australia-bugging-rex-patrick-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Rex Patrick’s latest transparency fight is over what he calls ‘most open secret in the history of Australian spying’ – maybe even the world</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A campaign to uncover any documents relating to whether <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2019/aug/10/witness-k-and-the-outrageous-spy-scandal-that-failed-to-shame-australia\">Australian spies bugged Timor-Leste</a> to gain the upper hand in sensitive oil and gas negotiations will be a little less secret after a critical win by the former senator Rex Patrick.</p><p>The politician turned transparency advocate is trying to finally lift the lid on the top-secret mission in 2004 that became a public scandal years later after an ex-spy and a former attorney general <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2015/may/04/east-timor-welcomes-australias-return-of-spying-documents-seized-by-asio\">attempted to mount a case in The Hague</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/31/timor-leste-australia-bugging-rex-patrick-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-31T00:04:51"
    }
